mmm, I like {.i'e} or variations to get more specific depending on what kind
of "cool" one is talking about.

e.g.  {.i'e} for a generic "I like/approve of this",  {.i'e .u'e} for
"that's awesome/amazing/etc...", {.i'e .io} for "that's
awesome/amazing/etc..." but with the connotation that I myself respect it.

All of this being more evidence that I would really benefit from peppering
my language with more UI (if I could get off my lazy ass and actually learn
them all in completion)

On Sun, Aug 8, 2010 at 1:16 AM, Lindar <lindarthebard@yahoo.com> wrote:

> > Shouldn't there be an exclamation indicator? even at the
> > observational? Just to be a little less unambiguous?
> > Just asking.
>
> You mean more unambiguous?
>
> Either way, we have {ba'e} and {sai} and a bunch of other things.
> I'm sure you could use those if you wanted.
